SRC/telewords -- telewords and telenum, as built for OS-9/68000===============================================================ORIG holds the post as comp.sources.misc carried it.  telewords.c buildsunchanged.  telenum.c gains four lines under #ifdef OSK redefining putcharas fputc: Microware's putchar macro evaluates its argument twice whenoutput goes to a pipe or a terminal, and `putchar(table[*currentStr++])'printed every other letter's digit there -- `telenum hello' gave 456.